DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(e^(x))/2");
$fun_1 = Formula("((ln(x))^4)+3");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((-infinity, 17] U ((5, infinity)) U ((-infinity, 17])) U (5, infinity)");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 17] U (5, infinity) U (-infinity, 17]");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(-infinity, 17] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [3, 5]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 17])");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{4, 6} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-8, 5}) U {-8, 5})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, 5})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-8, 5} U ({4, 6})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`8+16-13*3`] is equal to [_____]{Real(-15.)}
---

[`1+1+11+19*15`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(298.),width=>5}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{4, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, 5\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cap ((B) \cup B) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 17\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 5\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 4\}`]

Compute:
- [`(A \cup (C) \cup (A)) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cup C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap B \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, -5, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, 5, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 5, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-2, 5, 10>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -5, -6>") . Compute("<-2, 5, 10>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 5, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -5, -6>") x Compute("<-2, 5, 10>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-5, -5, -6>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, -3, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, -2, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, -3, -10>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<0, -2, 5>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, -3, -10>") . Compute("<0, -2, 5>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, -2, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, -2, 5>") . Compute("<3, -3, -10>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>3)}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
